{
  "dom_id": "step-q5418",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Given that a positive geometric sequence has \n${a}_{3}=12$, ${a}_{5}=3$ and ${a}_{k}=48$, what is the value of $k?$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we need to find the common ratio. We are told that ${a}_{3}=12$ and ${a}_{5}=3,$ so we can find the common ratio using a formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{n-m} & =\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}} \\\\ {r}^{5-3} & =\\frac{{a}_{5}}{{a}_{3}} \\\\ {r}^{5-3} & =\\frac{3}{12} \\\\ {r}^{2} & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ {r}^{2} & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\ r & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe disregard the negative solution since we are told that the sequence is positive.\n\nNow that we know the common ratio is $r=\\frac{1}{2}$, we can use the same formula to solve for the value of $k$ such that ${a}_{k}=48:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{n-m} & =\\frac{{a}_{n}}{{a}_{m}} \\\\ {r}^{k-3} & =\\frac{{a}_{k}}{{a}_{3}} \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{k-3} & =\\frac{48}{12} \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{k-3} & =4 \\\\ {(\\frac{1}{2})}^{k-3} & ={(\\frac{1}{2})}^{-2} \\\\ k-3 & =-2 \\\\ k & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
